{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "t-arch",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1180,
      "y": -560,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 60,
      "text": "## Architecture \u2014 how bytes become evidence"
    },
    {
      "id": "l0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1180,
      "y": -460,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### L0 \u00b7 raw\n`data/raw/` \u2014 exactly what the venue served, plus its published\nchecksum. Immutable.",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "l1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -860,
      "y": -460,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### L1 \u00b7 catalog\n`data/catalog/` \u2014 validated Parquet. Rebuildable from L0\nby `data build` alone.",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "reg",
      "type": "file",
      "x": -540,
      "y": -470,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 130,
      "file": "00-dashboard/generated/evidence.md",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "registry",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -220,
      "y": -460,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### registry.sqlite\nExperiments, trials, verdicts.\n**Trial history is append-only** \u2014 a deleted trial\nis a falsified experiment.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "pipe",
      "type": "file",
      "x": 100,
      "y": -470,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 130,
      "file": "00-dashboard/generated/pipeline.md",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "attn",
      "type": "file",
      "x": 420,
      "y": -470,
      "width": 260,
      "height": 130,
      "file": "00-dashboard/generated/attention.md",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "guards",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -540,
      "y": -280,
      "width": 900,
      "height": 90,
      "text": "### The guards, across every write path\n`guard_bash` venue + destructive \u00b7 `guard_write` CIO-only paths, L0, generated files\n`no_fabricated_numbers_pre` **denies** an unsupported number \u00b7 `no_fabricated_numbers` verifies what landed \u2014 [[ADR-013]]",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "t-flow",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1180,
      "y": -80,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 60,
      "text": "## Research flow \u2014 and where a human must act"
    },
    {
      "id": "idea",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1180,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### IDEA\n**HUMAN GATE \u2014 origination.**\nStrategy origination belongs to the CIO.\nAn agent may not start a programme.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "hyp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -890,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### Hypothesis\nPre-registered, committed to git\n*before* any result exists.\n`templates/hypothesis.md`",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "trials",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -600,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### Registered trials\n`exp register` then `exp run`.\nEvery run counts \u2014 including\nthe abandoned ones.",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "fals",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -310,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### Falsification\nKill tests run against authenticated\nevidence; the verdict is recorded in\nthe registry, not in a note.",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "promote",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -20,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### Promotion\n**HUMAN GATE.**\n`lifecycle promote` \u2014 the state machine\ndecides, never a file edit.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "capital",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 270,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### Capital\n**HUMAN GATE.**\nOnly the operator starts a live process.\nRisk limits are CIO-only.",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "kill",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 560,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### Kill switch\n**HUMAN GATE.**\n`06-risk/KILL` halts trading.\nAgents may not touch it.",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "e1",
      "type": "file",
      "x": -890,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 110,
      "file": "02-experiments/EXP-000001-btc-perp-funding-rate-reversal/EXP-000001.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "e2",
      "type": "file",
      "x": -600,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 240,
      "height": 110,
      "file": "02-experiments/EXP-000002-btc-trend-following-with-discrete-rebalancing/EXP-000002.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "judgment",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -310,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 530,
      "height": 110,
      "text": "### Judgment, not facts\nA killed line is a result. What it taught lives in\n[[DEC-000001]] \u00b7 [[DEC-000002]] \u00b7 [[LRN-000002]] \u00b7 [[LRN-000003]]",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "rule",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1180,
      "y": 380,
      "width": 1520,
      "height": 80,
      "text": "## The rule\n**Markdown holds judgment. `registry.sqlite` and hashed artifacts hold facts.**\nA note may argue and change its mind; it may not carry a trial count, a row count or a verdict.",
      "color": "3"
    }
  ],
